{
  "_note": "PR 2's two halves joined: a person's pick in the provider switcher (frontend lib/providerSwitch.ts) to the route client that runs it (backend execution/route_clients.py). Each case runs on a fixture node in route_client_definitions.json or on a real route-table node of the registry (PR 3). `saved` is what the node holds before the click, on top of every param's default; `keys` the key names set (values are fixtures); `wired` the input ports and what each carries (one edge each). `click` is a menu row id ('auto', a route id, '<route id>:plan'), 'alternative:<route id>' for the one-click switch under a stopped run, or null for no click. `switcher` is what the switcher shows before (`before`) and after the click, and `writes` the params the click changes on the saved node (snapped values included). Python (test_route_clients.py) saves `saved` + `writes` on the node and runs it through multi_route: `run.route` is the route the router picks, and `run.request` the one provider request it makes (`body` exactly, checked against `schema`), or `run.refused` the message it stops with before any request. TS (frontend/tests/components/switchToClient.test.tsx) seeds the node in the graph store, clicks the row in the Inspector's switcher and checks the store holds `saved` + `writes`, the card note is `notes`, and the switcher shows `switcher`. `click` may also be 'edit:<param>=<JSON value>', a person's edit of one setting in the Inspector or a pill (lib/providerSwitch.ts snapHidden on the shown route), or 'fix:<param>', the reset row under a stopped run (routeUnavailable fixes, applyFix). A `writes` value of null means the click cleared that param. PR 5: both twins compute every click's writes and notes (frontend tests/lib/providerSwitch.test.ts and test_route_clients.py test_switch_cases_snap_like_the_switcher, with node_route.snap_for_route / snap_hidden); the Inspector half (switchToClient.test.tsx) runs the row and alternative clicks.",
